          "type": "text",
          "importance": "supporting",
          "body": "Historical summaries connect the beginning of the boycott to the arrest of Florida A&M students Wilhelmina Jakes and Carrie Patterson after a dispute over bus seating in May 1956. Students and community members responded by refusing to ride. The precise sequence, wording of the charges and contemporary accounts remain to verify; this draft does not reproduce unverified quotations.",
