          "body": "Boycotting a transport system meant finding other ways to move. Community organizing included shared rides, walking and coordination among people who still needed to reach jobs and classes. Historical accounts describe the Inter-Civic Council as a central organizing body. Its membership, decisions and support networks should be checked through records that preserve participants’ own perspectives.",
